tion-pie":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/desperation-pie","n":"Desperation pie","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Desperation pies are pies in American cuisine made using staple ingredients like butter, sugar, eggs and flour, and making use of other ingredients that cooks had on hand to substitute for ingredients that were out of season or too expensive. These pies were more common before refrigeration and canned pie fillings, and during times of hardship like the Great Depression and rationing of World War II."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-desperation-pie"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desperation_pie"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/41/Buttermilk_Pie.jpg/500px-Buttermilk_Pie.jpg","w":500,"h":382,"by":"Ralph Daily","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buttermilk_Pie.jpg"}},"dish/grits-and-grunts":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/grits-and-grunts","n":"Grits and grunts","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Grits is a type of porridge made from coarsely ground dried corn (maize) or hominy, the latter being maize that has been treated with an alkali in a process called nixtamalization, with the pericarp (ovary wall) removed. It is eaten primarily in the United States. Grits are cooked in warm salted water or milk. They are often served with flavorings as a breakfast dish, though it is also served as a lunch or supper dish, particularly with meat.  Grits can be savory or sweet, with savory seasonings being more common. Grits are similar to other thick maize-based porridges from around the world, such as polenta, mieliepap, and mămăligă. Italian-Americans living in the delta of Arkansas and Mississippi recognized this and have substituted grits for traditional polenta dishes. The dish originated in the Southern United States but is now available nationwide. Grits are part of the dinner main di"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-grits-and-grunts"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grits_and_grunts"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/06/Grits1.jpg/500px-Grits1.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"sashafatcat","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grits1.jpg"}},"dish/inago-no-tsukudani":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/inago-no-tsukudani","n":"Inago no tsukudani","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Inago no tsukudani is a Japanese dish featuring rice grasshoppers that are boiled in soy sauce and sugar. Inago is the Japanese word for locust. The locusts are prepared in the \"tsukudani\" style of cooking (boiled in soy sauce and sugar). The dish is traditional in Japan's inland and mountain regions, including Nagano and Fukushima, where it once served as an important nutritional supplement."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-inago-no-tsukudani"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inago_no_tsukudani"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Grasshopper","ingredient/grasshopper"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Iekei ramen","dish/iekei-ramen"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Japanese cheesecake","dish/japanese-cheesecake"],["Japanese noodles","dish/japanese-no